mothershipOS: complete a playback buffer when the device has played it, not when it is copied into the device. A
sound card completes a period once it has been played; the backend completed the guest's buffers as soon as they
were in the device's ring, so every start drained what the guest had prefilled at once and the guest underran one
period later (Android: start, underrun, stop, prepare, start, ... endlessly: choppy audio). Written requests now wait
in `inflight` with the device position at their end and complete once frames written minus the device delay pass
it. The worker keeps running while requests are in flight; STOP and RELEASE return them too.

